# Exclude build outputs from the Docker build context. Without this,
# `docker build .` copies every prior ISO + chroot into the daemon,
# which trivially exceeds disk (Jul 19: v10 build ENOSPC'd on the
# 20G incremental/.build + 12G cx-distro/.build + 14G of old ISOs
# being pushed into the container context).
#
# Keep the Docker context lean — only source, manifests, and script
# files that Dockerfile.build actually needs. Docker cache still
# lives on the VM disk (unaffected by this ignore).

# Build outputs (regenerated every build)
incremental/.build/
cx-distro/.build/
cx-distro/rebuild/.build/

# ISOs (~5 GB each; several stack up across builds)
*.iso
ISO/
Testing_Reports/

# Model weights — NEVER go into Docker context (940 MB × N, embedded
# LATER by v6.manifest which runs on the host post-Docker). If a model
# reaches the container by accident it inflates every layer.
models/*.gguf

# Python caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Rust caches (live in $HOME/.cargo, not repo — belt-and-braces)
**/target/

# Node caches
node_modules/

# Editor + OS junk
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Git internals (Docker doesn't need the history)
.git/
.gitignore

# Local dev scratch
.agents/
teamwork_projects/
icebreaker-claude-state/
generate_book.py
Wallpaper*.png
test.sh
